    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0185" n="111" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg111"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/5552</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-27T01:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 27, 1917, 1 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11.15 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6544. My 6503, June 20,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d156-f1"/> and 6543, June 26.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d156-f2"/>
                    Sims sends me by special messenger from
                    Queenstown the most alarming reports of the submarine situation which are
                    confirmed by the Admiralty here. He says that the war will be won or lost in
                    this submarine zone within a few months. Time is the essence of the problem and
                        <pb facs="0186" n="112" xml:id="pg112"/> anti-submarine craft which cannot
                    be assembled in the submarine zone almost immediately may come too late. There
                    is therefore a possibility that this war may become a war between Germany and
                    the United States alone. Help is far more urgently and quickly needed in this
                    submarine zone than anywhere else in the whole war area.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
